  "step_3": "The decision reason requires evaluating outcomes based on probability > 1/2 (since there are two outcomes), and preferring the lottery with more probable outcomes. In this case, only A has a probable outcome (the -500€ outcome with 100% probability), while B has none (both outcomes have 50% probability, which is not greater than 0.5). Thus, A should be preferred according to the reason. However, the verbal report does not mention any such probabilistic threshold or analysis of probable outcomes. Instead, it references a subjective value judgment about getting money versus losing money, and a misrepresentation of the actual monetary outcomes (2000€ and 1000€ gift). The individual does not apply the rule of probable outcomes or compute the average of probable outcomes. Therefore, the decision reason was not used. The justification is based on emotional or subjective value, not on the formal rule of probable outcomes defined in the reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
}

